==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[carrom]]

===Etymology===
Probably corrupted from French {{term|carumboler|lang=fr}}, {{term|carambole|lang=fr}} being the red ball in [[billiards]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ˈkærʌm}}
* {{rhymes|ærʌm}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#{{context|cue sports|especially billiards}} A [[shot]] in which the [[ball]] [[struck]] with the [[cue]] comes in contact with two or more [[balls]] on the [[table]]; a hitting of two or more balls with the player's ball; in England it is called [[cannon]].

====Translations====
{{trans-top|(Billiards) A shot in which the ball struck with the cue comes in contact with two or more balls on the table}}
* Russian: {{t|ru|карамболь}}
{{trans-mid}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

#{{intransitive}} To make a carom.

